From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram_netlist -periphery verilog
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

-periphery verilog makes the block the core alone, <name>_core, and
writes the periphery to -wrapper_verilog as a module <name> around an
instance of it: the periphery's logic cells as assigns of their liberty
functions, for synthesis to map with the parent's logic, and its other
cells (clock gates, flops, ties) as instances. A net the core shares
with the periphery becomes a core port; a port only the periphery uses
leaves the core. The core is then outlined and pinned as with
-periphery unplaced. An option beside generator-built periphery, not a
replacement: which is better depends on how the array is integrated.

Tested: src/ram/test/periphery_verilog_asap7.tcl.

Commit 13 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
